module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineQcohPushforward.Colimits
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneration.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohLimits.Basic

/-!
# Directedness of the cardinally generated quasi-coherent subobjects of a module

Gabber's theorem (Stacks 077N) labels three assertions: the cardinal `κ` attached to a scheme,
the *directedness* of the category of quasi-coherent `κ`-generated subobjects of a
quasi-coherent module, and the statement that the canonical cocone of that category is
colimiting.  The first is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneration.cardinalBound`, already
proved.  This file proves the second, in the shape the source's "directed colimit" is expressed
by: `CardinalGeneratedQuasicoherentSubobject F (cardinalBound X)` is a filtered category.

## Main definitions

* `joinSubobject G H`: the join of two subobjects of a module on a scheme, realized as the
  subobject cut out by the image of `G ⊕ H ⟶ F`.  It is the upper bound used for directedness;
  `Subobject.sup` would do as well, but its underlying object is reached only through the
  thin-skeleton quotient, whereas `joinSubobject` comes with the epimorphism
  `joinEpi` out of the coproduct, which is what both the quasi-coherence and the bound on the
  generators are read off from.
* `gsOfEpi`, `gsComp`, `gsCoprod`: families of generating sections obtained from an
  epimorphism out of a free module, from an epimorphism out of a module already generated, and
  from a pair of generated modules.

## Main results

* `isCardinalGenerated_of_restrict` and `exists_restrict_generatingSections`: the two
  directions of the scheme-level reading of `IsCardinalGenerated`, namely as an open covering
  together with `κ`-bounded generating sections of the restriction of the module to each
  member.
* `isCardinalGenerated_of_isZero`: a zero module is `κ`-generated, for every `κ`.
* `isCardinalGenerated_of_epi_coprod`: **the closure property that directedness rests on.**
  For an infinite `κ`, a quotient of the direct sum of two `κ`-generated modules is
  `κ`-generated.  The covering is the family of pairwise intersections of the two given
  coverings, over which both modules are generated by at most `κ` sections at once.
* `isQuasicoherent_joinSubobject` and `isCardinalGenerated_joinSubobject`: the join of two
  quasi-coherent `κ`-generated subobjects is again one.
* `cardinalGeneratedQuasicoherentSubobject_isFiltered`: **Stacks 077N, the directedness
  assertion.**

## Implementation notes

`IsFiltered` needs three things; two of them are free here.  `Subobject F` is a thin category,
so any two parallel morphisms of subobjects are equal and the coequalizing-morphism condition
holds with the identity; and the nonemptiness is the zero subobject `⊥`, whose underlying
object is initial (`CategoryTheory.Subobject.botCoeIsoInitial`) hence quasi-coherent, because
quasi-coherence is closed under colimits of every shape, the empty one included.  All the
content is therefore in the existence of a common upper bound.

Of the three bounds proved beside `cardinalBound`, only `aleph0_le_cardinalBound` is used: the
bound `κ + κ = κ` on the index type `σ.I ⊕ τ.I` of the combined generators needs `κ` infinite,
and nothing else about `cardinalBound X` enters.  The colimit assertion, which is where
`mk_affineOpens_le_cardinalBound` and `mk_sections_le_cardinalBound` are needed, is **not**
proved here.

Several instances are supplied positionally.  `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.ofEpi` and
`CategoryTheory.Limits.epi_comp` take their epimorphism as an instance argument, and on
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` — a `def` for `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf` carrying its
own `Category` instance — instance search does not see through to the epimorphisms produced by
the lemmas below; `gsComp` therefore takes `Epi` as an explicit argument, and
`CategoryTheory.Limits.epi_comp` is applied with its seven leading arguments positional.
`CategoryTheory.Limits.PreservesColimitPair.iso` needs `PreservesColimitsOfSize.{0, 0}`, the
shape `Discrete WalkingPair` living in `Type 0`, so the `.{u, u}` instance that
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor` has from its adjunction is shrunk by hand.
Finally, `Cardinal.mk (gs ..).I ≤ κ` must not be attacked by `rw`: the projection `.I` of a
`GeneratingSections` on an open subscheme carries `V.toScheme.ringCatSheaf`, whose type is
`TopCat.Sheaf RingCat _` rather than `CategoryTheory.Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology _) _`,
and the two agree only after unfolding, so instance search inside `rw` fails; the bounds below
are passed as terms, where the defeq is checked at the transparency of term elaboration.

## Not proved here

The remaining assertion of tag 077N, that
`cardinalGeneratedQuasicoherentSubobjectCocone F (cardinalBound X)` is a colimit cocone, is
open.  That is the assertion for which `cardinalBound X` must be adequate, and the route to it
runs through `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.exists_bounded_compatible_family` and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.sheafSubmodule`, whose quasi-coherence and bound on
local generators are also still open.  Nothing below uses either of those, so the directedness
assertion is independent of them.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 077N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/077N)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 077L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/077L)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits SheafOfModules TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneration

/-! ### Generating sections from an epimorphism -/

section Generic

variable {C : Type*} [Category C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {R : CategoryTheory.Sheaf J RingCat.{u}} [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- An epimorphism from a free sheaf of modules is a family of generating sections.  Every
morphism out of a free module is `freeHomEquiv.symm` of its family of sections, so no condition
beyond surjectivity is involved. -/
def gsOfEpi {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {I : Type u} (φ : SheafOfModules.free I ⟶ M)
    (hφ : Epi φ) : M.GeneratingSections where
  I := I
  s := M.freeHomEquiv φ
  epi := by rw [Equiv.symm_apply_apply]; exact hφ

/-- The generating sections `gsOfEpi φ hφ` are indexed by the index type of the free module. -/
@[simp]
theorem gsOfEpi_I {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {I : Type u} (φ : SheafOfModules.free I ⟶ M)
    (hφ : Epi φ) : (gsOfEpi φ hφ).I = I :=
  rfl

/-- The images of a family of generating sections under an epimorphism generate the target.
This is `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.ofEpi` with the epimorphism taken as an explicit
argument. -/
def gsComp {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (σ : M.GeneratingSections) (p : M ⟶ N) (hp : Epi p) :
    N.GeneratingSections :=
  gsOfEpi (σ.π ≫ p) (@epi_comp _ _ _ _ _ _ σ.epi _ hp)

/-- The generating sections `gsComp σ p hp` are indexed by the index type of `σ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem gsComp_I {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (σ : M.GeneratingSections) (p : M ⟶ N)
    (hp : Epi p) : (gsComp σ p hp).I = σ.I :=
  rfl

end Generic

/-- A coproduct of two epimorphisms is an epimorphism.  Proved by cancelling against the two
inclusions; Mathlib records this for coproducts over an arbitrary index only through
colimit preservation, which is unavailable for the two category structures on sheaves of
modules over a scheme. -/
theorem epi_coprodMap {C : Type*} [Category C] {A B A' B' : C} [HasBinaryCoproduct A B]
    [HasBinaryCoproduct A' B'] (f : A ⟶ A') (g : B ⟶ B') (hf : Epi f) (hg : Epi g) :
    Epi (coprod.map f g) := by
  constructor
  intro Z a b hab
  refine coprod.hom_ext ?_ ?_
  · exact hf.left_cancellation _ _ (by simpa using congrArg (fun t => coprod.inl ≫ t) hab)
  · exact hg.left_cancellation _ _ (by simpa using congrArg (fun t => coprod.inr ≫ t) hab)

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- Two families of generating sections give one for the direct sum, indexed by the disjoint
union of the two index types. -/
def gsCoprod {M N : X.Modules} (σ : M.GeneratingSections) (τ : N.GeneratingSections) :
    (M ⨿ N).GeneratingSections :=
  gsOfEpi ((SheafOfModules.freeSumIso (R := X.ringCatSheaf) σ.I τ.I).inv ≫ coprod.map σ.π τ.π)
    (@epi_comp _ _ _ _ _ _ (IsIso.epi_of_iso _) _ (epi_coprodMap σ.π τ.π σ.epi τ.epi))

/-- The generating sections `gsCoprod σ τ` are indexed by the disjoint union `σ.I ⊕ τ.I`. -/
@[simp]
theorem gsCoprod_I {M N : X.Modules} (σ : M.GeneratingSections) (τ : N.GeneratingSections) :
    (gsCoprod σ τ).I = (σ.I ⊕ τ.I) :=
  rfl

/-! ### Cardinal generation read on an open covering -/

/-- A module generated, over each member of an open covering, by at most `κ` sections of its
restriction, is `κ`-generated. -/
theorem isCardinalGenerated_of_restrict (M : X.Modules) {I : Type u} (U : I → X.Opens)
    (hU : IsOpenCover U) {κ : Cardinal.{u}}
    (σ : ∀ i, (M.restrict (U i).ι).GeneratingSections)
    (hσ : ∀ i, Cardinal.mk (σ i).I ≤ κ) : IsCardinalGenerated (R := X.ringCatSheaf) M κ :=
  ⟨localGeneratorsDataOfRestrict M U hU σ, hσ⟩

/-- Conversely, a `κ`-generated module has an open covering over each member of which its
restriction is generated by at most `κ` sections. -/
theorem exists_restrict_generatingSections (M : X.Modules) {κ : Cardinal.{u}}
    (h : IsCardinalGenerated (R := X.ringCatSheaf) M κ) :
    ∃ (I : Type u) (U : I → X.Opens) (_ : IsOpenCover U)
      (σ : ∀ i, (M.restrict (U i).ι).GeneratingSections), ∀ i, Cardinal.mk (σ i).I ≤ κ := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := h
  exact ⟨d.I, d.X, (Opens.coversTop_iff _ d.X).mp d.coversTop,
    fun i => generatingSectionsOfOver (d.X i) M (d.generators i), hd⟩

/-- A zero module is generated by the empty family, hence is `κ`-generated for every `κ`. -/
theorem isCardinalGenerated_of_isZero {M : X.Modules} (hM : IsZero M) (κ : Cardinal.{u}) :
    IsCardinalGenerated (R := X.ringCatSheaf) M κ := by
  have h2 : IsZero ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor (⊤ : X.Opens).ι).obj M) :=
    Functor.map_isZero _ hM
  refine isCardinalGenerated_of_restrict M (fun _ : PUnit.{u + 1} => (⊤ : X.Opens))
    (IsOpenCover.mk (by simp))
    (fun _ => gsOfEpi (I := PEmpty.{u + 1}) (h2.from_ _) ⟨fun _ _ _ => h2.eq_of_src _ _⟩)
    (fun _ => ?_)
  exact le_trans (le_of_eq (Cardinal.mk_eq_zero PEmpty.{u + 1})) (by simp)

/-- The disjoint union of two types of size at most an infinite `κ` has size at most `κ`. -/
theorem mk_sum_le {κ : Cardinal.{u}} (hκ : Cardinal.aleph0 ≤ κ) (I K : Type u)
    (h1 : Cardinal.mk I ≤ κ) (h2 : Cardinal.mk K ≤ κ) : Cardinal.mk (I ⊕ K) ≤ κ := by
  rw [Cardinal.mk_sum]
  exact Cardinal.add_le_of_le hκ (by simpa using h1) (by simpa using h2)

/-- The pairwise intersections of two open coverings form an open covering. -/
theorem isOpenCover_inf {I K : Type u} {A : I → X.Opens} {B : K → X.Opens} (hA : IsOpenCover A)
    (hB : IsOpenCover B) : IsOpenCover (fun p : I × K => A p.1 ⊓ B p.2) := by
  refine IsOpenCover.mk ?_
  have h1 : ⨆ p : I × K, (A p.1 ⊓ B p.2) = ⨆ i, ⨆ j, (A i ⊓ B j) := iSup_prod
  rw [h1]
  simp only [← inf_iSup_eq, hB.iSup_eq_top, inf_top_eq]
  exact hA.iSup_eq_top

/-- Restriction to an open subscheme is a left adjoint, hence preserves epimorphisms. -/
theorem epi_restrictFunctor_map {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ Y) [IsOpenImmersion f]
    {M N : Y.Modules} (p : M ⟶ N) (hp : Epi p) :
    Epi ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor f).map p) :=
  (inferInstance : (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor f).PreservesEpimorphisms).preserves p

/-- Restriction to an open subscheme commutes with binary direct sums. -/
def restrictCoprodIso {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ Y) [IsOpenImmersion f] (M N : Y.Modules) :
    ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor f).obj M ⨿ (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor f).obj N) ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor f).obj (M ⨿ N) :=
  haveI : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{0, 0} (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor f) :=
    preservesColimitsOfSize_shrink _
  PreservesColimitPair.iso _ M N

/-- The comparison isomorphism `restrictCoprodIso f M N` is in particular an epimorphism. -/
theorem epi_restrictCoprodIso_hom {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ Y) [IsOpenImmersion f]
    (M N : Y.Modules) : Epi (restrictCoprodIso f M N).hom :=
  have _h : IsIso (restrictCoprodIso f M N).hom := Iso.isIso_hom _
  IsIso.epi_of_iso _

/-- Generating sections of the restriction of a quotient of `M ⊕ N` to an open, from generating
sections of the restrictions of `M` and of `N`. -/
def gsRestrictOfEpiCoprod {M N P : X.Modules} (e : M ⨿ N ⟶ P) (he : Epi e) (V : X.Opens)
    (σ : (M.restrict V.ι).GeneratingSections) (τ : (N.restrict V.ι).GeneratingSections) :
    (P.restrict V.ι).GeneratingSections :=
  gsComp (gsCoprod σ τ)
    ((restrictCoprodIso V.ι M N).hom ≫ (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor V.ι).map e)
    (@epi_comp _ _ _ _ _ _ (epi_restrictCoprodIso_hom V.ι M N) _
      (epi_restrictFunctor_map V.ι e he))

/-- The generating sections `gsRestrictOfEpiCoprod e he V σ τ` are indexed by `σ.I ⊕ τ.I`. -/
@[simp]
theorem gsRestrictOfEpiCoprod_I {M N P : X.Modules} (e : M ⨿ N ⟶ P) (he : Epi e) (V : X.Opens)
    (σ : (M.restrict V.ι).GeneratingSections) (τ : (N.restrict V.ι).GeneratingSections) :
    (gsRestrictOfEpiCoprod e he V σ τ).I = (σ.I ⊕ τ.I) :=
  rfl

/-- **A quotient of the direct sum of two `κ`-generated modules is `κ`-generated**, for `κ`
infinite.  Over the intersection of a member of a covering generating `M` with a member of a
covering generating `N`, the two families together generate `M ⊕ N`, hence their images
generate the quotient; and the disjoint union of two index types of size at most `κ` has size
at most `κ` because `κ` is infinite. -/
theorem isCardinalGenerated_of_epi_coprod {M N P : X.Modules} (e : M ⨿ N ⟶ P) (he : Epi e)
    {κ : Cardinal.{u}} (hκ : Cardinal.aleph0 ≤ κ)
    (hM : IsCardinalGenerated (R := X.ringCatSheaf) M κ)
    (hN : IsCardinalGenerated (R := X.ringCatSheaf) N κ) :
    IsCardinalGenerated (R := X.ringCatSheaf) P κ := by
  obtain ⟨I, A, hA, σ, hσ⟩ := exists_restrict_generatingSections M hM
  obtain ⟨K, B, hB, τ, hτ⟩ := exists_restrict_generatingSections N hN
  refine isCardinalGenerated_of_restrict P (fun p : I × K => A p.1 ⊓ B p.2)
    (isOpenCover_inf hA hB)
    (fun p => gsRestrictOfEpiCoprod e he _
      (generatingSectionsRestrictLE M inf_le_left (σ p.1))
      (generatingSectionsRestrictLE N inf_le_right (τ p.2))) (fun p => ?_)
  exact mk_sum_le hκ _ _ (hσ p.1) (hτ p.2)

/-! ### The join of two subobjects -/

variable {F : X.Modules}

/-- The sum of the inclusions of two subobjects of `F`. -/
abbrev joinDesc (G H : Subobject F) : ((G : X.Modules) ⨿ (H : X.Modules)) ⟶ F :=
  coprod.desc G.arrow H.arrow

/-- **The join of two subobjects of a module on a scheme**: the subobject cut out by the image
of the sum of their inclusions. -/
def joinSubobject (G H : Subobject F) : Subobject F :=
  Subobject.mk (Abelian.image.ι (joinDesc G H))

/-- The canonical epimorphism from the direct sum of two subobjects onto their join. -/
def joinEpi (G H : Subobject F) :
    ((G : X.Modules) ⨿ (H : X.Modules)) ⟶ ((joinSubobject G H : Subobject F) : X.Modules) :=
  Abelian.factorThruImage (joinDesc G H) ≫ (Subobject.underlyingIso _).inv

/-- The morphism `joinEpi G H` from the direct sum of two subobjects onto their join is an
epimorphism. -/
theorem epi_joinEpi (G H : Subobject F) : Epi (joinEpi G H) :=
  have h1 : Epi (Abelian.factorThruImage (joinDesc G H)) := inferInstance
  have h2 : Epi (Subobject.underlyingIso (Abelian.image.ι (joinDesc G H))).inv := inferInstance
  @epi_comp _ _ _ _ _ _ h1 _ h2

/-- A subobject lies below its join with another one. -/
theorem le_joinSubobject_left (G H : Subobject F) : G ≤ joinSubobject G H :=
  Subobject.le_mk_of_comm (coprod.inl ≫ Abelian.factorThruImage (joinDesc G H))
    (by simp [joinDesc, coprod.inl_desc])

/-- A subobject lies below the join of another one with it. -/
theorem le_joinSubobject_right (G H : Subobject F) : H ≤ joinSubobject G H :=
  Subobject.le_mk_of_comm (coprod.inr ≫ Abelian.factorThruImage (joinDesc G H))
    (by simp [joinDesc, coprod.inr_desc])

/-- The direct sum of two quasi-coherent subobjects is quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_coprod (M N : X.Modules) (hM : M.IsQuasicoherent)
    (hN : N.IsQuasicoherent) : (M ⨿ N).IsQuasicoherent :=
  QuasicoherentColimits.isQuasicoherent_colimit (pair M N) (by rintro ⟨_ | _⟩ <;> assumption)

/-- The join of two quasi-coherent subobjects of a quasi-coherent module is quasi-coherent: it
is the image of a morphism between quasi-coherent modules, hence a kernel of a cokernel of
one. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_joinSubobject [F.IsQuasicoherent] (G H : Subobject F)
    (hG : (G : X.Modules).IsQuasicoherent) (hH : (H : X.Modules).IsQuasicoherent) :
    ((joinSubobject G H : Subobject F) : X.Modules).IsQuasicoherent := by
  have hsum : ((G : X.Modules) ⨿ (H : X.Modules)).IsQuasicoherent :=
    isQuasicoherent_coprod _ _ hG hH
  have hker : (Abelian.image (joinDesc G H)).IsQuasicoherent :=
    have : (cokernel (joinDesc G H)).IsQuasicoherent := inferInstance
    QcohLimits.isQuasicoherent_kernel (cokernel.π (joinDesc G H))
  exact (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf).prop_of_iso
    (Subobject.underlyingIso (Abelian.image.ι (joinDesc G H))).symm hker

/-- The join of two `κ`-generated subobjects is `κ`-generated, for `κ` infinite. -/
theorem isCardinalGenerated_joinSubobject {κ : Cardinal.{u}} (hκ : Cardinal.aleph0 ≤ κ)
    (G H : Subobject F)
    (hG : IsCardinalGenerated (R := X.ringCatSheaf) (G : X.Modules) κ)
    (hH : IsCardinalGenerated (R := X.ringCatSheaf) (H : X.Modules) κ) :
    IsCardinalGenerated (R := X.ringCatSheaf)
      ((joinSubobject G H : Subobject F) : X.Modules) κ :=
  isCardinalGenerated_of_epi_coprod (joinEpi G H) (epi_joinEpi G H) hκ hG hH

/-! ### Directedness -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 077N.**  For the common cardinal bound of a scheme, the category of
bounded quasi-coherent subobjects of every quasi-coherent module is filtered. -/
@[stacks 077N "directedness"]
instance cardinalGeneratedQuasicoherentSubobject_isFiltered (X : Scheme.{u}) (F : X.Modules)
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] :
    IsFiltered (CardinalGeneratedQuasicoherentSubobject F (cardinalBound X)) where
  cocone_objs G H :=
    ⟨⟨joinSubobject G.obj H.obj,
      isQuasicoherent_joinSubobject G.obj H.obj G.property.1 H.property.1,
      isCardinalGenerated_joinSubobject (aleph0_le_cardinalBound X) G.obj H.obj
        G.property.2 H.property.2⟩,
      ObjectProperty.homMk (le_joinSubobject_left G.obj H.obj).hom,
      ObjectProperty.homMk (le_joinSubobject_right G.obj H.obj).hom, trivial⟩
  cocone_maps _ Y f g := ⟨Y, 𝟙 Y, by rw [ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (Subsingleton.elim f.hom g.hom)]⟩
  nonempty := ⟨⟨⊥,
    have h : IsInitial ((⊥ : Subobject F) : X.Modules) :=
      IsInitial.ofIso initialIsInitial Subobject.botCoeIsoInitial.symm
    QuasicoherentColimits.isQuasicoherent_of_isColimit (D := Functor.empty X.Modules)
      (fun k => PEmpty.elim k.as) h,
    isCardinalGenerated_of_isZero
      (IsZero.of_iso (isZero_zero X.Modules) (Subobject.botCoeIsoZero)) _⟩⟩

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGeneration

end
